      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T14:17:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I thought vmbase in theory can be used by a multi-threaded client.\n\nI agree that this should be a long-term goal but we currently have none of the necessary support.\n\nFor example, see how our TLS (if I can call it this way) is setup in assembly: [once and for all](http://cs/android/packages/modules/Virtualization/vmbase/entry.S?l\u003d163).\n\nWe don\u0027t have support for context switching, thread states, or (assuming multi-threading beyond SMP) getting other CPUs out of \"reset stand-by\" and lots of work would need to go into making `vmbase` support that use-case.\n\nOnce that\u0027s done, making `errno` thread-local should be straight forward.",
      "parentUuid": "d46ce7e5_aafd1797",
